1
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:34,960
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:37,950
[Episode 13]

3
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:08,639
It's very sweet.

4
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:10,750
I'll save this honey for you.

5
00:02:11,190 --> 00:02:12,850
You can have as much as you want

6
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,090
after your mission.

7
00:02:18,079 --> 00:02:19,910
My time recovering here

8
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,710
has been like

9
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:26,280
five years ago

10
00:02:27,079 --> 00:02:27,960
in Hangzhou.

11
00:02:29,150 --> 00:02:30,470
From now on, in Hangzhou,

12
00:02:30,470 --> 00:02:32,280
you are my husband, Sun Cheng,

13
00:02:33,590 --> 00:02:34,870
and I am Mrs. Sun.

14
00:02:38,030 --> 00:02:40,470
What is Mr. Sun like in his daily life?

15
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,090
For example,

16
00:02:45,870 --> 00:02:47,630
Li Qing has a huge sweet tooth.

17
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:50,750
Honey and sugar-roasted chestnuts

18
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:52,350
are her absolute favorites,

19
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:54,630
but she rarely gets to have them.

20
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:57,680
Sun Cheng

21
00:02:59,030 --> 00:03:00,310
likes to drink.

22
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,800
Drinking?

23
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,190
I can learn.

24
00:03:09,710 --> 00:03:10,520
It's fine.

25
00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:12,310
You can just drink soup.

26
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:26,240
Uncle Hai will take you there.

27
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:08,800
See you next time.

28
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:13,000
Will we see each other again?

29
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:14,240
Of course.

30
00:04:26,630 --> 00:04:27,920
You told me

31
00:04:32,070 --> 00:04:34,270
drinking soup is living a life,

32
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,320
and drinking alcohol

33
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:40,930
is having something on your mind.

34
00:04:44,090 --> 00:04:46,620
But I really miss those days
of drinking soup.

35
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:55,680
Me too.

36
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:39,159
Come on, look at the camera.

37
00:05:39,159 --> 00:05:39,960
Look this way.

38
00:05:40,159 --> 00:05:41,090
A little closer.

39
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:42,780
As a married couple should be.

40
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:44,360
Right, come on.

41
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,830
Three, two, one.

42
00:05:50,630 --> 00:05:51,360
Liu Xia.

43
00:05:52,070 --> 00:05:53,530
Why are you standing here?

44
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:54,830
Take your medicine.

45
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:06,630
Water.

46
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:11,750
Go back to your ward,

47
00:06:12,070 --> 00:06:13,470
or you might catch a cold.

48
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:30,500
Zhou Xue, won't you come out
for some exercise?

49
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:47,560
Go ahead.

50
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,170
Come on, Liu Xia.

51
00:06:49,310 --> 00:06:50,040
Keep up.

52
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:50,830
Come on.

53
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,310
You got one. Well done.

54
00:06:55,310 --> 00:06:56,000
You got one.

55
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:56,560
Keep it up, Liu Xia.

56
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:57,000
Next.

57
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,070
Come on, keep up.

58
00:06:58,630 --> 00:06:59,490
You got one too?

59
00:07:00,750 --> 00:07:02,240
Well done. Slow down.

60
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:03,240
Come on.

61
00:07:03,630 --> 00:07:05,160
Next. Everyone gets a turn.

62
00:07:11,750 --> 00:07:12,480
Time to eat.

63
00:07:37,830 --> 00:07:38,880
What is it?

64
00:07:39,510 --> 00:07:40,430
A math problem?

65
00:07:43,350 --> 00:07:44,350
What's your name?

66
00:07:48,570 --> 00:07:49,700
Know how to solve it?

67
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,120
Are you Mr. Ishida?

68
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,560
I'm from No. 76.

69
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,630
Mr. Kagesa invites you over.

70
00:08:07,950 --> 00:08:09,630
Mr. Kagesa is looking for me?

71
00:08:10,070 --> 00:08:10,720
Yes.

72
00:08:38,030 --> 00:08:38,750
Who are you?

73
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:41,000
Mr. Ishida,

74
00:08:41,549 --> 00:08:42,549
don't be afraid.

75
00:08:43,750 --> 00:08:46,950
All you need to do is cooperate
and answer a few questions.

76
00:08:47,150 --> 00:08:48,280
I don't understand.

77
00:08:49,910 --> 00:08:51,040
I don't understand.

78
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,920
I know your Chinese is very good.

79
00:08:57,270 --> 00:08:59,530
Cooperating with me is your only way out.

80
00:09:01,950 --> 00:09:03,360
Where is Ms. Ou Yang?

81
00:09:07,910 --> 00:09:08,640
I don't know.

82
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:13,760
Do you remember now?

83
00:09:16,130 --> 00:09:17,260
Do you remember now?

84
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,440
Mr. Ishida,

85
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:31,800
you should know what's good for you.

86
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:35,370
I know you want to go back to Japan.

87
00:09:36,750 --> 00:09:38,810
As long as you tell me where Ou Yang is,

88
00:09:40,150 --> 00:09:42,750
I can make the call right now
and let you go back.

89
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,790
But if you keep on like this,

90
00:09:48,910 --> 00:09:50,710
I can only send you to Chongqing.

91
00:09:51,670 --> 00:09:52,390
Over there,

92
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:55,120
I won't be the one calling the shots.

93
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:03,790
Just kill me.

94
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:17,460
You said he's a coward.

95
00:10:18,050 --> 00:10:19,180
He's very stubborn.

96
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:22,790
I think

97
00:10:23,950 --> 00:10:26,010
we should just send him to Chongqing.

98
00:10:30,010 --> 00:10:30,930
Say something.

99
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:33,750
If we keep dawdling like this,

100
00:10:33,750 --> 00:10:36,150
the Japanese will find out
sooner or later.

101
00:10:42,390 --> 00:10:43,590
Let me think about it.

102
00:10:45,030 --> 00:10:46,090
What are you doing?

103
00:10:47,030 --> 00:10:47,870
Do me a favor.

104
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,060
I don't want to get married right now.

105
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:52,840
We'll talk about that later.

106
00:10:53,030 --> 00:10:54,490
You'll go see someone now.

107
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:55,230
Who?

108
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:59,060
It's too lonely being alone.

109
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:04,180
Here's someone to keep you company.

110
00:11:14,250 --> 00:11:15,010
Mr. Ishida.

111
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,910
Did they send you to get close to me

112
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:20,750
to find out about Ou Yang?

113
00:11:22,870 --> 00:11:24,400
I'm not a member of the NBIS.

114
00:11:25,910 --> 00:11:27,390
I just want you to live.

115
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:29,920
I won't believe you anymore.

116
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:46,000
I tried. Didn't work.

117
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,960
You beat him up like that.

118
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:53,300
How is that any different from No. 76?

119
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:55,960
To achieve our goal,

120
00:11:57,790 --> 00:11:59,200
we use certain means.

121
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,060
Is there a problem?

122
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:02,790
Besides,

123
00:12:03,510 --> 00:12:04,510
he's Japanese.

124
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:05,650
I can beat him up.

125
00:12:06,710 --> 00:12:08,370
Cut the crap and make him talk.

126
00:12:09,810 --> 00:12:11,720
You beat him up like that
and he didn't talk.

127
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,650
How am I supposed to get him to talk?

128
00:12:13,750 --> 00:12:15,610
Then your friend will have to die.

129
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,780
I heard the Japanese like to
commit seppuku.

130
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:27,730
In a moment, I'm going to use this knife

131
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:31,240
to cut his belly open.

132
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:35,030
I'm going to see

133
00:12:36,510 --> 00:12:39,110
if the Japanese really have
black intestines.

134
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,580
Then go ahead and cut mine open too.

135
00:12:42,580 --> 00:12:44,040
You think I wouldn't dare?

136
00:12:55,860 --> 00:12:57,590
Take a break from the violence.

137
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:00,970
You're not just helping me.

138
00:13:01,510 --> 00:13:02,840
You're helping him too.

139
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,550
He doesn't trust me anymore.

140
00:13:06,550 --> 00:13:07,670
He won't tell me.

141
00:13:10,670 --> 00:13:11,730
You're a smart man,

142
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:13,520
and you know him well.

143
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:15,700
You'll find a way to make him talk.

144
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,090
I can't think of any.

145
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,270
Why do I feel like

146
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,670
you don't really want him to talk?

147
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:26,230
I really have no idea how to.

148
00:13:26,630 --> 00:13:28,030
Just let me go.

149
00:13:28,630 --> 00:13:29,840
For a Japanese,

150
00:13:30,750 --> 00:13:31,750
is it worth it?

151
00:13:37,030 --> 00:13:38,360
Are you going to kill me?

152
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:46,080
I can kill him.

153
00:13:59,910 --> 00:14:01,030
I told them

154
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:03,640
to give you one more night

155
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:06,410
to save your life for now.

156
00:14:28,270 --> 00:14:29,930
Involving irrelevant people

157
00:14:30,270 --> 00:14:32,000
in our important project

158
00:14:33,910 --> 00:14:35,110
is against the rules.

159
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:38,790
Captain Tao,

160
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:40,710
what do you mean?

161
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:45,270
I'm not sure if this Chen guy

162
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:48,440
is really working for us.

163
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,480
Do you have a better idea?

164
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:00,700
Anyway, if he doesn't cooperate,

165
00:15:04,270 --> 00:15:05,510
I'll kill him.

166
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:11,670
Fine.

167
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:14,580
Then I'll kill you.

168
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:20,750
Ishida didn't return to Japan.

169
00:15:22,060 --> 00:15:25,150
How much does he know
about Project Slumber?

170
00:15:25,670 --> 00:15:29,840
He was one of the original members
of Project Slumber.

171
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:33,600
He is very important to our research work.

172
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:37,910
I will find him.

173
00:15:40,630 --> 00:15:43,560
I sent someone to ask the person
in charge of the ship.

174
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:47,670
He didn't board the ship at all.

175
00:15:49,670 --> 00:15:52,320
So Mr. Ishida hasn't left Shanghai?

176
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,550
We've searched the lab and his place.

177
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:59,080
There's no sign that he's been back.

178
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:01,630
There're only two possible reasons why
Mr. Ishida changed his itinerary

179
00:16:01,630 --> 00:16:02,690
at the last minute.

180
00:16:03,510 --> 00:16:04,640
Either he defected,

181
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:07,320
or he was kidnapped.

182
00:16:08,630 --> 00:16:11,030
He wouldn't defect. It's a kidnapping.

183
00:16:12,630 --> 00:16:14,440
Judging from the way it's done,

184
00:16:15,270 --> 00:16:17,670
it should be the work of
the Hurricane Team.

185
00:16:19,480 --> 00:16:20,810
I remember not long ago,

186
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:23,270
Director Li and Captain Du

187
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:26,170
had already wiped out the Hurricane Team,

188
00:16:26,630 --> 00:16:28,760
and I requested commendation for you.

189
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:30,670
Looks like

190
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:33,650
there were some
that slipped through the net.

191
00:16:33,750 --> 00:16:35,150
Please rest assured, General,

192
00:16:35,150 --> 00:16:37,000
I will definitely find Ishida.

193
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,440
Alive? Or dead?

194
00:16:42,390 --> 00:16:43,670
Find him,

195
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:45,440
dead or alive.

196
00:16:52,870 --> 00:16:54,630
Be quick and give the Japanese something.

197
00:16:54,630 --> 00:16:56,360
Make that woman shut her mouth.

198
00:16:57,150 --> 00:16:58,550
Rest assured, Director.

199
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:00,600
If it really is the Hurricane Team,

200
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:01,800
I know how to find him.

201
00:17:02,750 --> 00:17:05,400
According to Plum Blossom Agency,

202
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:06,880
before Ishida left,

203
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:08,640
he went to Fumin Hospital

204
00:17:09,030 --> 00:17:10,160
to see an old friend.

205
00:17:11,550 --> 00:17:12,349
An old friend?

206
00:17:13,109 --> 00:17:13,920
Ou Yang.

207
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:16,349
Hoshino's former secretary.

208
00:17:16,349 --> 00:17:17,609
She later went insane.

209
00:17:18,310 --> 00:17:20,640
The Plum Blossom Agency
was worried she'd leak secrets,

210
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:23,569
so they temporarily put her
in the psychiatric ward.

211
00:17:23,829 --> 00:17:25,829
Got it. I'll look into it right away.

212
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:31,930
The Propaganda Section said
Chen Kailai hasn't come to work today.

213
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:35,350
Ishida suddenly got kidnapped.

214
00:17:35,350 --> 00:17:37,640
Chen Kailai hasn't come to work.

215
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:42,030
This is definitely no coincidence.

216
00:17:43,750 --> 00:17:46,410
Could it be that they caught
Chen Kailai as well?

217
00:17:49,030 --> 00:17:50,160
Have someone keep an eye out.

218
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:52,160
Let me know immediately
when Chen Kailai comes back.

219
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:52,790
Yes.

220
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:17,410
You seem to like snow very much.

221
00:18:22,390 --> 00:18:24,320
Is it because your name is Zhou Xue,

222
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:27,960
and it has the word "snow" in it?

223
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:36,200
My name is Liu Xia.

224
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,130
Liu Xia (homophone of "stay").

225
00:18:46,590 --> 00:18:49,920
You only stay in the hospital
if your illness can't be cured.

226
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:51,840
This name is unlucky.

227
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:59,000
So my name is not Liu Xia.

228
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,760
And your name is not Zhou Xue.

229
00:19:03,590 --> 00:19:04,720
Your name is Ou Yang.

230
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:09,140
Then what is your name?

231
00:19:13,570 --> 00:19:14,630
My name is Musheng.

232
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:18,160
Musheng,

233
00:19:20,590 --> 00:19:22,390
hope this letter finds you well.

234
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:25,310
I came across your photos

235
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:26,900
and really liked them.

236
00:19:28,350 --> 00:19:29,950
I, too, wanted to be like you,

237
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:32,220
going to the battlefield to do my part

238
00:19:32,270 --> 00:19:33,530
and make a difference.

239
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:36,520
But it's no longer possible.

240
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:39,680
I have to leave China with my family.

241
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,640
Hello, Ou Yang.

242
00:19:44,130 --> 00:19:45,960
Thank you for liking my photos.

243
00:19:46,510 --> 00:19:49,370
I heard the cherry blossoms
in Japan are beautiful,

244
00:19:49,530 --> 00:19:52,140
but I haven't seen them with my own eyes.

245
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:56,210
Musheng, hope this letter finds you well.

246
00:19:57,270 --> 00:19:59,480
I really miss everything in China.

247
00:20:00,750 --> 00:20:01,750
Your photos

248
00:20:01,770 --> 00:20:03,970
are my only comfort in Japan.

249
00:20:38,310 --> 00:20:39,510
Who are you, exactly?

250
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:41,270
You can hear me out first

251
00:20:41,270 --> 00:20:43,200
and then decide if you want to go on.

252
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:44,640
I told you,

253
00:20:45,590 --> 00:20:46,750
Musheng sent me.

254
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:51,800
It's just around the corner.

255
00:20:52,110 --> 00:20:53,970
He showed you the letters I wrote?

256
00:20:54,550 --> 00:20:56,210
Twenty-six letters in total.

257
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:59,060
"Musheng, hope this letter
finds you well."

258
00:21:00,030 --> 00:21:00,890
This sentence,

259
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:03,160
you wrote it twenty-six times in total.

260
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:06,370
He copied every single letter of yours

261
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:07,750
into his notebook.

262
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:11,680
Musheng never gave up on you.

263
00:21:13,950 --> 00:21:15,460
He sent me to save you.

264
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:23,920
Zhou Xue, are you asleep?

265
00:21:24,860 --> 00:21:25,990
I'm coming in, okay?

266
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:34,110
Zhou Xue.

267
00:21:39,300 --> 00:21:40,430
This is Mr. Du.

268
00:21:48,830 --> 00:21:49,890
Don't take me away.

269
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:51,540
Don't take me away.

270
00:21:52,110 --> 00:21:53,170
Don't take me away.

271
00:21:54,610 --> 00:21:56,270
He's not taking you away or arresting you.

272
00:21:56,270 --> 00:21:57,680
Mr. Du just wants to ask you
a few questions.

273
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:59,010
He'll leave after that.

274
00:22:01,510 --> 00:22:02,270
May I ask

275
00:22:03,310 --> 00:22:04,960
if you know where Ishida is?

276
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:08,750
Ishida?

277
00:22:11,100 --> 00:22:12,030
I don't know him.

278
00:22:14,190 --> 00:22:16,630
He's Dr. Hoshino's student.

279
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:18,160
Hoshino?

280
00:22:21,110 --> 00:22:22,550
Hoshino can read minds.

281
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,880
He knows what you're thinking.

282
00:22:27,240 --> 00:22:29,000
Hoshino stole my brain.

283
00:22:31,590 --> 00:22:33,320
I'm not talking about Hoshino.

284
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:35,310
It's Ishida.

285
00:22:35,510 --> 00:22:36,790
Right, Ishida.

286
00:22:37,550 --> 00:22:39,150
Hoshino sent you to catch me?

287
00:22:41,240 --> 00:22:42,400
Don't take me away!

288
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:44,070
Don't take me away!

289
00:22:44,070 --> 00:22:45,510
-Okay. Okay.
-Don't take me away!

290
00:22:45,510 --> 00:22:47,030
Okay, okay, he won't.

291
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:48,720
I told you.

292
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:49,940
She can't help you.

293
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:18,520
Please, Mr. Du.

294
00:23:33,790 --> 00:23:35,440
So this is Musheng.

295
00:23:36,270 --> 00:23:37,870
You mentioned in your letter

296
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:39,910
that you wanted a photo of him.

297
00:23:41,270 --> 00:23:42,440
The negative of the photo

298
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:44,240
was kept in his notebook.

299
00:23:46,750 --> 00:23:47,480
I think

300
00:23:48,270 --> 00:23:49,730
it might have been for you.

301
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:54,100
Good thing he didn't send it to me.

302
00:23:54,880 --> 00:23:57,080
Before I could go to Hangzhou to see him,

303
00:23:57,160 --> 00:23:58,220
the Japanese came.

304
00:24:23,310 --> 00:24:25,680
A few letters were not destroyed in time

305
00:24:25,960 --> 00:24:28,160
and fell into the hands of the Japanese.

306
00:24:28,700 --> 00:24:30,630
So I couldn't trust you at first.

307
00:24:36,030 --> 00:24:38,160
Let's formally introduce ourselves.

308
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:39,940
I am "Su Causeway,"

309
00:24:40,350 --> 00:24:41,410
Musheng's friend.

310
00:24:45,960 --> 00:24:47,220
You are "Su Causeway."

311
00:24:47,640 --> 00:24:49,510
Then what about him?

312
00:24:50,830 --> 00:24:51,830
"Broken Bridge."

313
00:24:53,070 --> 00:24:54,130
He once mentioned,

314
00:24:55,270 --> 00:24:57,070
his name was given by his mother.

315
00:24:57,590 --> 00:24:59,070
He lacked wood in the Five Elements,

316
00:24:59,070 --> 00:25:00,400
so he was named Musheng.

317
00:25:01,350 --> 00:25:02,480
"Broken Bridge"...

318
00:25:03,880 --> 00:25:06,610
The character for "bridge"
also has "wood" in it.

319
00:25:09,110 --> 00:25:10,590
But why did you come

320
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:12,860
instead of him?

321
00:25:18,070 --> 00:25:18,960
He's dead.

322
00:25:23,110 --> 00:25:23,920
Is he?

323
00:25:41,510 --> 00:25:44,400
She used to be Hoshino's assistant too.

324
00:25:44,790 --> 00:25:45,990
Later she went insane

325
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:48,000
and the Japanese locked her up here.

326
00:25:51,070 --> 00:25:52,930
She probably knows some secrets.

327
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:55,400
I remember the female Communist
we caught before

328
00:25:55,400 --> 00:25:56,800
was also looking for her.

329
00:25:57,720 --> 00:25:59,720
Now that you mention it, I remember.

330
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:00,920
It's true.

331
00:26:01,880 --> 00:26:02,510
Boss,

332
00:26:02,510 --> 00:26:04,840
have the Communists gotten involved too?

333
00:26:06,140 --> 00:26:10,200
Kidnapping Ishida doesn't seem like
something the Communists would do.

334
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:12,120
But we have to be on guard.

335
00:26:12,540 --> 00:26:13,460
Send a few men

336
00:26:14,270 --> 00:26:15,320
to keep an eye on Fumin Hospital.

337
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:16,050
Understood.

338
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:35,330
Have some water.

339
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:36,350
Thank you.

340
00:26:44,110 --> 00:26:45,000
In Japan,

341
00:26:45,290 --> 00:26:48,220
I was researching vaccine production
with Hoshino.

342
00:26:48,750 --> 00:26:50,000
But later I found out

343
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:53,130
the purpose of that research
was not that simple.

344
00:27:01,110 --> 00:27:01,880
I'm sorry.

345
00:27:02,030 --> 00:27:02,920
I'm sorry.

346
00:27:03,370 --> 00:27:04,370
Be careful.

347
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:05,160
Sorry.

348
00:27:17,350 --> 00:27:19,610
I could tell from years of lab experience

349
00:27:20,070 --> 00:27:22,510
that those were not animal test data.

350
00:27:23,520 --> 00:27:24,750
The numbers on it

351
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:27,480
were all obtained through
human experiments.

352
00:27:29,110 --> 00:27:32,550
They were data from in vivo experiments
on Chinese people.

353
00:27:36,240 --> 00:27:38,170
Musheng gave me some information.

354
00:27:38,440 --> 00:27:40,160
The plagues that broke out
in several places in China

355
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:41,590
also confirmed my guess.

356
00:27:43,830 --> 00:27:45,030
But I was too scared.

357
00:27:47,300 --> 00:27:48,430
I was an accomplice.

358
00:27:51,380 --> 00:27:53,640
I would never be able to
atone for my sins.

359
00:27:59,680 --> 00:28:01,140
The letters Musheng wrote

360
00:28:02,270 --> 00:28:03,110
saved me.

361
00:28:04,720 --> 00:28:07,320
He strengthened my resolve
to return to China.

362
00:28:08,480 --> 00:28:09,200
Ou Yang,

363
00:28:10,110 --> 00:28:11,910
hope this letter finds you well.

364
00:28:12,270 --> 00:28:15,330
I can feel the hardships
you're going through in Japan,

365
00:28:15,720 --> 00:28:18,320
as well as your helplessness
and frustration.

366
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:21,590
Because I am just as powerless as you.

367
00:28:22,550 --> 00:28:23,720
Our country

368
00:28:23,720 --> 00:28:24,960
is the same.

369
00:28:25,480 --> 00:28:27,480
There is no hope in sight.

370
00:28:28,550 --> 00:28:29,750
Shanghai has fallen,

371
00:28:30,270 --> 00:28:34,000
followed by Nanjing and Hangzhou.

372
00:28:34,960 --> 00:28:36,240
I am a photographer.

373
00:28:36,720 --> 00:28:38,510
The camera is my gun.

374
00:28:39,310 --> 00:28:41,030
In times of national crisis,

375
00:28:41,510 --> 00:28:43,160
no matter who we are

376
00:28:43,440 --> 00:28:44,570
or what we have done,

377
00:28:45,110 --> 00:28:47,570
we should all do our part
to save the country.

378
00:28:48,110 --> 00:28:49,400
Even if our contribution

379
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:51,270
may seem very small,

380
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:54,920
it is still a great one.

381
00:28:55,750 --> 00:28:57,010
I want to do something.

382
00:28:58,920 --> 00:29:00,960
I know I must do something.

383
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:03,350
I want to save this country

384
00:29:03,350 --> 00:29:05,150
from its suffering in my own way.

385
00:29:08,110 --> 00:29:10,480
I also know why you came to see me.

386
00:29:11,740 --> 00:29:15,160
You want to learn about Hoshino's research
through me, right?

387
00:29:15,160 --> 00:29:16,960
The research is nearing its end.

388
00:29:19,030 --> 00:29:20,110
We too suspect

389
00:29:21,030 --> 00:29:22,510
that this is a large-scale
biological attack

390
00:29:22,510 --> 00:29:24,040
targeting Chinese people.

391
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:28,790
I hope you can help us

392
00:29:30,370 --> 00:29:31,720
stop this project.

393
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:45,310
The work he didn't finish,

394
00:29:49,670 --> 00:29:51,000
I will finish it for him.

395
00:30:50,820 --> 00:30:51,660
Before I die,

396
00:30:52,400 --> 00:30:55,130
I probably won't have the chance
to see her again.

397
00:30:59,070 --> 00:30:59,930
If she is found,

398
00:31:00,710 --> 00:31:01,510
there will be.

399
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:10,090
They promised me

400
00:31:11,160 --> 00:31:12,960
that as long as they find Ou Yang,

401
00:31:13,510 --> 00:31:14,640
they won't kill you.

402
00:31:20,950 --> 00:31:22,480
But she's already gone mad.

403
00:31:25,380 --> 00:31:26,940
It was all my fault.

404
00:31:38,220 --> 00:31:39,950
Did you see her in China?

405
00:31:42,310 --> 00:31:43,440
She rejected me.

406
00:31:46,880 --> 00:31:47,640
Listen.

407
00:31:48,400 --> 00:31:51,440
Our country gave her
the most advanced education,

408
00:31:51,600 --> 00:31:54,750
yet she is not loyal to us.

409
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:58,350
This kind of woman is not worthy of you.

410
00:32:02,310 --> 00:32:06,440
Do you think she will betray us?

411
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:11,310
She met a pen pal.

412
00:32:14,830 --> 00:32:15,680
I think

413
00:32:19,070 --> 00:32:20,400
she might betray us.

414
00:32:24,140 --> 00:32:25,100
I ruined her.

415
00:32:28,270 --> 00:32:30,830
I deserve to die for my sin.

416
00:32:43,750 --> 00:32:45,030
I've had my last meal.

417
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:50,860
Let them do it as soon as possible.

418
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:16,000
I'll have a chat with Mr. Ishida.

419
00:33:17,310 --> 00:33:18,200
Out you go.

420
00:33:33,960 --> 00:33:35,000
Mr. Ishida,

421
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:38,830
those who die with sins

422
00:33:39,110 --> 00:33:40,510
cannot go to heaven.

423
00:33:46,750 --> 00:33:48,640
Now is your chance to atone.

424
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:53,530
I think her illness
is mostly psychological.

425
00:33:53,640 --> 00:33:55,370
She will never get better here.

426
00:33:56,350 --> 00:33:57,830
Tell us where Ou Yang is,

427
00:33:58,680 --> 00:34:00,540
and we will take her to Chongqing.

428
00:34:01,590 --> 00:34:03,250
She will get proper treatment

429
00:34:04,270 --> 00:34:05,550
and may even recover.

430
00:34:06,920 --> 00:34:07,590
Of course,

431
00:34:09,630 --> 00:34:11,230
you will also be able to live.

432
00:34:17,920 --> 00:34:18,670
Otherwise,

433
00:34:19,550 --> 00:34:21,550
I will have to take you to Chongqing.

434
00:34:22,480 --> 00:34:23,810
A lose-lose situation—

435
00:34:24,070 --> 00:34:24,929
why go for that?

436
00:34:32,360 --> 00:34:35,230
Mr. Ishida, you probably don't want
to be separated from your family

437
00:34:35,230 --> 00:34:36,400
forever, right?

438
00:34:41,400 --> 00:34:42,630
Will you cure her?

439
00:34:44,070 --> 00:34:45,800
I never make promises lightly.

440
00:35:03,370 --> 00:35:04,300
Fumin Hospital,

441
00:35:06,480 --> 00:35:07,540
Psychiatric Ward,

442
00:35:10,480 --> 00:35:11,630
Room 203.

443
00:35:15,190 --> 00:35:17,920
Du Huangqiao has already
been to Fumin Hospital.

444
00:35:23,030 --> 00:35:24,630
He is already wary of Ou Yang

445
00:35:24,940 --> 00:35:27,600
and left secret sentries from No. 76
at the door.

446
00:35:29,190 --> 00:35:31,050
We need to act as soon as possible.

447
00:35:37,400 --> 00:35:38,730
Let him go back to Japan.

448
00:35:41,920 --> 00:35:43,070
I only promised you

449
00:35:44,440 --> 00:35:45,960
to spare his life for now.

450
00:35:51,050 --> 00:35:52,340
Can I go home now?

451
00:35:59,280 --> 00:36:00,680
When are you coming back?

452
00:36:05,230 --> 00:36:07,490
What should I say if people ask about you?

453
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:13,070
I will go back

454
00:36:13,760 --> 00:36:15,220
when things are done here.

455
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:20,360
You mind your own business.

456
00:36:22,610 --> 00:36:24,010
If I wanted to betray you,

457
00:36:24,570 --> 00:36:26,300
I'd have had plenty of chances.

458
00:36:26,480 --> 00:36:28,340
I wouldn't have waited until now.

459
00:36:29,510 --> 00:36:30,320
You know,

460
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:33,480
it's no use if I'm the only one

461
00:36:34,110 --> 00:36:34,970
who trusts you.

462
00:36:40,320 --> 00:36:41,190
Take me home!

463
00:36:53,590 --> 00:36:55,320
He knows the rules pretty well.

464
00:37:02,320 --> 00:37:03,980
What should we do with Ishida?

465
00:37:06,830 --> 00:37:08,960
Chen Kailai wants me to spare his life.

466
00:37:10,630 --> 00:37:12,630
Are you really going to do as he says?

467
00:37:12,800 --> 00:37:13,550
If we let the Japanese go,

468
00:37:13,550 --> 00:37:15,210
wouldn't that sell us all out?

469
00:37:17,510 --> 00:37:20,040
Sparing his life doesn't mean
letting him go.

470
00:37:20,880 --> 00:37:22,210
If Ou Yang gets rescued,

471
00:37:23,360 --> 00:37:25,290
we'll send them both to Chongqing.

472
00:37:25,920 --> 00:37:27,120
If she isn't rescued,

473
00:37:28,030 --> 00:37:30,630
we'll hand him over to Chongqing
to fulfill our obligation.

474
00:37:30,630 --> 00:37:32,130
Whatever Chongqing decides to do with him

475
00:37:32,130 --> 00:37:33,390
is none of my business.

476
00:37:34,770 --> 00:37:36,430
And I will have kept my promise

477
00:37:37,060 --> 00:37:38,060
to Chen Kailai.

478
00:37:40,840 --> 00:37:42,700
If you really value him that much,

479
00:37:43,670 --> 00:37:45,400
you should recruit him.

480
00:37:47,230 --> 00:37:48,360
I've said it before.

481
00:37:49,710 --> 00:37:50,960
He's not like us.

482
00:37:51,760 --> 00:37:52,890
How is he different?

483
00:37:55,070 --> 00:37:56,360
He's a photographer.

484
00:37:57,240 --> 00:37:57,960
An artist?

485
00:38:04,710 --> 00:38:06,590
Affection can kill anyone.

486
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:09,890
"God of Wealth,"

487
00:38:11,330 --> 00:38:13,590
don't ever let a man
get the better of you.

488
00:38:35,320 --> 00:38:36,450
Where are you going?

489
00:38:39,440 --> 00:38:40,440
To get breakfast.

490
00:38:41,150 --> 00:38:42,360
Breakfast is ready for you.

491
00:38:42,360 --> 00:38:44,290
Now that you're back, don't leave.

492
00:38:44,590 --> 00:38:45,590
Why?

493
00:38:48,440 --> 00:38:49,960
Ms. Jin ordered

494
00:38:50,070 --> 00:38:51,190
that you rest well.

495
00:38:51,950 --> 00:38:52,980
If you run around,

496
00:38:53,030 --> 00:38:54,070
I'll lose my job.

497
00:39:03,760 --> 00:39:05,670
How much is Jinbao paying you?

498
00:39:06,480 --> 00:39:07,610
I'll pay you double.

499
00:39:09,440 --> 00:39:10,110
Sir,

500
00:39:10,510 --> 00:39:12,030
it's not about the money.

501
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:14,440
Ms. Jin will kill me.

502
00:39:16,760 --> 00:39:17,710
Okay, I got it.

503
00:39:20,820 --> 00:39:22,800
Chen Kailai is back at the photo studio.

504
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:23,650
He said he's sick

505
00:39:23,650 --> 00:39:24,980
and needs a few days off.

506
00:39:31,920 --> 00:39:33,120
Should I go fetch him?

507
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:35,190
No need.

508
00:39:35,920 --> 00:39:37,760
He won't tell the truth anyway.

509
00:39:59,360 --> 00:40:01,230
The phone is disconnected.

510
00:40:05,070 --> 00:40:07,550
Ms. Jin asked to disconnect it
for a few days.

511
00:40:08,510 --> 00:40:09,640
Who are you calling?

512
00:40:10,440 --> 00:40:11,800
I need to call a customer

513
00:40:12,340 --> 00:40:13,170
to let him know

514
00:40:13,510 --> 00:40:15,110
his expedited photos are ready.

515
00:40:15,110 --> 00:40:16,110
If you disconnect the phone,

516
00:40:16,110 --> 00:40:17,510
how am I supposed to notify him?

517
00:40:17,510 --> 00:40:19,070
Are we still running a business?

518
00:40:19,070 --> 00:40:21,800
I haven't seen any customers
these past few days.

519
00:40:23,110 --> 00:40:24,890
Just because you don't have customers

520
00:40:24,890 --> 00:40:26,090
doesn't mean I don't.

521
00:40:28,190 --> 00:40:28,920
Mr. Zhao.

522
00:40:28,940 --> 00:40:30,550
Mr. Chen, how's business lately?

523
00:40:30,550 --> 00:40:33,230
We're still counting on friends like you
to keep us going.

524
00:40:33,230 --> 00:40:33,830
By the way,

525
00:40:33,980 --> 00:40:35,780
I was just about to come find you.

526
00:40:37,440 --> 00:40:38,550
Well...

527
00:40:41,550 --> 00:40:43,630
Meng's photos are ready.

528
00:40:43,840 --> 00:40:45,550
Thanks for rushing them out.

529
00:40:46,150 --> 00:40:47,280
I heard you got sick.

530
00:40:47,550 --> 00:40:48,680
How are you feeling?

531
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:51,320
Just a bit of insomnia and a headache.

532
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:52,760
Nothing serious.

533
00:40:53,550 --> 00:40:54,950
Captain Du came to see me.

534
00:40:55,430 --> 00:40:57,360
It seems everyone cares about you.

535
00:40:57,540 --> 00:40:59,140
Inspector Su is worried too.

536
00:40:59,710 --> 00:41:00,510
I know.

537
00:41:01,280 --> 00:41:02,760
Tell Inspector Su

538
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:04,690
I'll be able to go to work soon.

539
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:06,070
Right, Xin Xiang?

540
00:41:07,170 --> 00:41:07,780
Yes.

541
00:41:08,070 --> 00:41:09,850
Mr. Chen will recover very soon.

542
00:41:09,850 --> 00:41:11,960
Okay, let's meet up when you recover.

543
00:41:12,070 --> 00:41:13,070
Okay, take care.

544
00:41:48,780 --> 00:41:51,180
NBIS has located Ou Yang
at Fumin Hospital.

545
00:41:56,920 --> 00:41:57,590
Who are you?

546
00:41:58,920 --> 00:42:00,320
Liu Xia's family member.

547
00:42:14,550 --> 00:42:16,840
Liu Xia, your father is here to see you.

548
00:42:19,670 --> 00:42:21,550
How are you feeling, hon?

549
00:42:23,760 --> 00:42:24,630
I'm doing well.

550
00:42:25,470 --> 00:42:27,000
I'm ready to be discharged.

551
00:42:29,110 --> 00:42:30,240
I'll leave you to it.

552
00:42:34,670 --> 00:42:35,360
Uncle Hai.

553
00:42:36,070 --> 00:42:37,960
Ou Yang has agreed to cooperate
and leave with us.

554
00:42:37,960 --> 00:42:39,290
We can leave at any time.

555
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:40,920
But did you notice

556
00:42:40,920 --> 00:42:42,820
that the guards at the stairs
have been changed?

557
00:42:42,820 --> 00:42:44,440
Du Huangqiao came last night.

558
00:42:44,440 --> 00:42:46,570
The guards were changed this morning.

559
00:42:46,960 --> 00:42:48,820
They must be his secret sentries.

560
00:42:48,960 --> 00:42:51,240
Looks like NBIS has zeroed in
on this place.

561
00:42:51,240 --> 00:42:52,190
They act fast

562
00:42:52,220 --> 00:42:53,970
and could snatch Ou Yang at any moment.

563
00:42:53,970 --> 00:42:55,010
This adds

564
00:42:55,070 --> 00:42:57,130
another layer of uncertainty for us.

565
